/*!
\page page_stepdhit StEpdHit

\brief Calibrated hit from a single scintillator tile in the STAR Event Plane Detector.

\section epdhit_overview Overview

StEpdHit stores the gain-corrected signal from one tile of the **Event Plane Detector (EPD)**.
The EPD has 744 plastic scintillator tiles on two wheels (East and West) covering
2.1 < |η| < 5.1.  Each tile is read out by a silicon photomultiplier (SiPM) and a
QT charge-integrating board.  One StEpdHit is created per good tile per event.

The object carries three payloads (10 bytes total):
- a packed tile identifier (side, super-sector, tile number),
- packed QT-board data (ADC, TAC, TDC, flags), and
- a gain-calibrated energy loss \c nMIP (in units of the Landau MPV for one MIP).

\section epdhit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StEpdHit
\endcode

StEpdHit objects are stored in \ref page_stepdepdcollection via \c StSPtrVecEpdHit
and retrieved with \c StEvent::epdCollection().

\section epdhit_id Tile Identification

The signed 16-bit member \c mId encodes the complete tile address:

| Quantity | Computation |
|----------|-------------|
| Side | sign(\c mId): +1 = West, −1 = East |
| Super-sector position | \c abs(mId) / 100, range [1,12] |
| Tile number | \c abs(mId) % 100, range [1,31] |

Tiles 1–9 are small (inner ring, higher |η|); tiles 10–31 are large (outer ring).

\section epdhit_qtdata QT-Board Packing

The 32-bit \c mQTdata word packs:

| Bits | Field |
|------|-------|
| 0–11 | ADC [0,4095] |
| 12–23 | TAC [0,4095] |
| 24–28 | TDC [0,31] |
| 29 | hasTAC flag |
| 30 | database good/bad status |

\section epdhit_members Data Members

| Type | Member | Description |
|------|--------|-------------|
| \c Short_t | \c mId | Packed tile ID (sign = side, abs = 100×position + tile) |
| \c Int_t | \c mQTdata | Packed QT-board word (ADC, TAC, TDC, flags) |
| \c Float_t | \c mnMIP | Gain-calibrated energy in units of one MIP Landau MPV |
| \c Int_t | \c mTruthId | MC truth GEANT track ID of the primary energy-deposit particle |

\section epdhit_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c id() | Signed tile ID |
| \c side() | +1 (West) or −1 (East) |
| \c position() | Super-sector index [1,12] |
| \c tile() | Tile number within super-sector [1,31] |
| \c adc() | Raw ADC [0,4095] |
| \c tac() | TAC value (valid if \c hasTac()) |
| \c tdc() | TDC value [0,31] |
| \c hasTac() | True if TAC is measured |
| \c nMIP() | Gain-corrected energy (MIP units) |
| \c isGood() | True if tile is good in the database |
| \c idTruth() | MC truth particle GEANT ID |

\section epdhit_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StEpdCollection* epdColl = event->epdCollection();
for (const StEpdHit* hit : epdColl->hits()) {
    if (!hit->isGood()) continue;
    float nMIP = hit->nMIP();
    int   side = hit->side();   // +1 West, -1 East
    int   pos  = hit->position();
    int   tile = hit->tile();
    bool  isSmall = (tile <= 9);
    // accumulate event-plane Q-vector ...
}
\endcode

\see StEpdCollection, StEvent
*/
